{"id": "35238", "revid": "2240936", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=35238", "title": "Tamura", "text": "Tamura (\u7530\u6751\u5e02 \"Tamura-shi\") is a city in the Fukushima Prefecture, in Honshu, Japan. Tamura was founded in 2005 as a result of a merger of several smaller towns and villages. Funehiki, Miyakoji, Ogoe, Takine, and Tokiwa all now exist as Tamura city. Tamura's sister city is Mansfield, Ohio.\nUnderstand.\nTourist Information Site.\nThe city has a Japanese-only guide site.\nGet in.\nThe Banetsu East (\u78d0\u8d8a\u6771, Ban-etsu-to, or Ban-to) Line from Koriyama makes stops in Kanameta, Funehiki, Iwaki-tokiwa, Ogoe, Sugaya, and Kammata within Tamura city."}
